WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.395
Lesson 14.3.

00:00:02.395 --> 00:00:07.111
Operating procedures: multisig signing, change control, reviews.

00:00:07.111 --> 00:00:08.864
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:08.864 --> 00:00:10.410
be able to run your bank with

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.781
procedures that prevent single-point mistakes.

00:00:14.081 --> 00:00:15.371
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.371 --> 00:00:17.056
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.056 --> 00:00:19.771
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.771 --> 00:00:21.296
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:23.458
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:28.318
transaction (destination, amount, calldata) on their own

00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:31.053
device screen, not a shared screenshot.

00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:34.344
written up (thesis, risk register row, size)

00:00:34.344 --> 00:00:37.423
and waits 24h before execution. First,

00:00:37.423 --> 00:00:39.931
Multisig signing procedure: every signer

00:00:39.931 --> 00:00:42.678
independently verifies the. Next, Change

00:00:42.678 --> 00:00:45.833
control: new protocol, new chain, new

00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:48.541
strategy, or a cap change is.

00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:51.688
Then, Separation: the person proposing a

00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:54.751
vault transaction isn't the only one

00:00:54.751 --> 00:00:58.863
approving it. And finally, Review calendar: weekly books

00:00:58.863 --> 00:01:02.254
· monthly register · quarterly stress test and

00:01:02.254 --> 00:01:05.501
recovery drill · annual review (Module 13.5).

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.316
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:09.316 --> 00:01:14.046
A 2-of-3 vault moves $40,000 to the operating wallet.

00:01:14.046 --> 00:01:17.745
Signer 1 proposes; Signer 2 checks the destination against

00:01:17.745 --> 00:01:21.193
the allowlist and the amount against the ladder refill

00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:24.816
schedule on their hardware wallet screen, then signs.

00:01:24.816 --> 00:01:26.666
Logged in the books with both names.

00:01:27.966 --> 00:01:29.426
Here's your checklist.

00:01:29.426 --> 00:01:30.961
Do it now, for real.

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:34.086
First, Signing procedure written for every signer.

00:01:34.086 --> 00:01:37.851
Next, Change-control template and 24h rule.

00:01:37.851 --> 00:01:39.926
And finally, Review calendar set.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:42.436
Question 1.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:44.481
Why verify on your own device screen?

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.736
The answer: Screens and screenshots can be faked;

00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:54.911
the hardware display shows what you're actually signing.

00:01:56.211 --> 00:01:57.456
Question 2.

00:01:57.456 --> 00:01:58.961
What is change control for?

00:02:03.381 --> 00:02:05.727
The answer: Forcing new risks through

00:02:05.727 --> 00:02:08.321
thesis, register and a cooling-off period.

00:02:09.621 --> 00:02:10.891
Question 3.

00:02:10.891 --> 00:02:12.956
How often is the stress test re-run?

00:02:17.376 --> 00:02:20.192
The answer: Quarterly, and after big changes.

00:02:21.492 --> 00:02:22.737
Let's recap.

00:02:22.737 --> 00:02:27.567
Multisig signing procedure: every signer independently verifies the.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.668
Change control: new protocol, new chain, new

00:02:30.668 --> 00:02:32.966
strategy, or a cap change is.

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:36.358
Separation: the person proposing a vault transaction

00:02:36.358 --> 00:02:38.706
isn't the only one approving it.

00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:42.640
Review calendar: weekly books · monthly register

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.092
· quarterly stress test and recovery drill

00:02:46.092 --> 00:02:48.501
· annual review (Module 13.5).

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.315
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:52.315 --> 00:02:57.060
Next up, Lesson 14.4: Operator capstone and certification.
